{"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity","doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph"]]},"metadata":{"fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"stronglyConnectedComponents","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Components","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:12Connectivity10ComponentsV"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"role":"symbol","externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P12ConnectivityE27stronglyConnectedComponentsAD0G0VyxGyF","extendedModule":"GraphProtocols","symbolKind":"method","title":"stronglyConnectedComponents()","roleHeading":"Instance Method","remoteSource":{"fileName":"StronglyConnectedComponents.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Connectivity\/StronglyConnectedComponents.swift#L136"},"modules":[{"name":"Connectivity","relatedModules":["GraphProtocols"]}]},"abstract":[{"text":"The strongly connected components: maximal sets of vertices each reaching every other.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Tarjan’s algorithm, iterative, O(V + E).","type":"text"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/stronglyConnectedComponents()","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"stronglyConnectedComponents","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/Components","text":"Components","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:12Connectivity10ComponentsV"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"discussion","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Discussion"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Components are in the order Tarjan’s algorithm completes them, on a depth-first search"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with roots in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" order and successors in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"successors(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":" order (the order of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"NetworkX, petgraph and Boost). That is a reverse topological order of the condensation:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"every edge between components goes from a later component to an earlier one, so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reversed()"},{"type":"text","text":" lists the components with every edge going forward. Each component lists its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertices in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" order."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Each component’s first vertex is its earliest in ","type":"text"},{"code":"vertices","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so on a graph whose vertex","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"positions are insertion order (","type":"text"},{"code":"StableDirectedGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"), one sort puts the components in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"insertion order:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let inInsertionOrder = graph.stronglyConnectedComponents().sorted { graph.vertices.firstIndex(of: $0.first!)! < graph.vertices.firstIndex(of: $1.first!)! }"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"kind":"symbol","variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/connectivity\/graphprotocols\/directe